{"analysis_support":"supported","claim_id":"convoluted|lexicalised_participle","effective_disposition":"advance","endorsement_override":false,"endorsements":6,"input_digest":"af0e0f1a06b6782f96dd18bc1c8a503dc9a47dd4959dfd30763e2d458da71fb9","label_status":"human-validated","meanings":[{"predictability":"predictable","sense_id":"oewn-convoluted__5.00.00.coiled.00"},{"predictability":"not_predictable","sense_id":"oewn-convoluted__5.00.00.complex.00"}],"morphology_disposition":"advance","note":"The meaning 'rolled longitudinally upon itself' is directly derivable from the root 'convolute' meaning 'curl, wind, or twist together' plus the adjectival '-ed' suffix, and the root itself is recorded with the same adjectival sense. The meaning 'highly complex or intricate and occasionally devious' is a figurative extension not directly derivable from the physical sense of 'curl, wind, or twist together'. While the root's sense of 'practice sophistry; change the meaning' hints at deviousness, the full complex/intricate sense is a metaphorical drift beyond the literal parts.","partition":"development","review_decision":"accepted","rubric_version":"morphology-rubric/2","slice":"lexicalised_participle","validated_at":"2026-08-30T06:43:23.462Z"}
{"analysis_support":"supported","claim_id":"fruitfulness|affix_strip","effective_disposition":"advance","endorsement_override":false,"endorsements":0,"input_digest":"731b3241e95e27bac87b08a4c3b4bee829ce9ac2cfd4747186ee089069210684","label_status":"human-validated","meanings":[{"predictability":"predictable","sense_id":"oewn-fruitfulness__1.07.00.."},{"predictability":"not_predictable","sense_id":"oewn-fruitfulness__1.09.00.."}],"morphology_disposition":"advance","note":"The meaning 'the quality of something that causes or assists healthy growth' is directly the quality of being 'productive or conducive to producing in abundance', as the root adjective describes. The suffix '-ness' simply nominalizes this quality. The meaning 'the intellectual productivity of a creative imagination' is a figurative extension of the root's literal sense of producing abundance. While the root's general sense of productivity is present, the specific application to intellectual or creative output is not directly derivable from the root's definition alone.","partition":"development","review_decision":"accepted","rubric_version":"morphology-rubric/2","slice":"affix_strip","validated_at":"2026-08-30T06:44:49.299Z"}
{"analysis_support":"supported","claim_id":"handspring|compound_split","effective_disposition":"exclude","endorsement_override":false,"endorsements":0,"input_digest":"3151bc48c9e8afddb10b2db85c9d059a6995b67d5c040f1206eb85668b7a7241","label_status":"human-validated","meanings":[{"predictability":"predictable","sense_id":"oewn-handspring__1.04.00.."}],"morphology_disposition":"exclude","note":"The acrobatic feat is literally a spring (leap) performed on the hands, so a learner knowing 'hand' and 'spring' (as a leap) could arrive at this meaning.","partition":"development","review_decision":"accepted","rubric_version":"morphology-rubric/2","slice":"stress","validated_at":"2026-08-30T06:45:17.456Z"}
{"analysis_support":"supported","claim_id":"mercurial|meaning_shift_derivation","effective_disposition":"advance","endorsement_override":false,"endorsements":9,"input_digest":"39c8ef6857710750368f1b36b97c945e29da36b6a4175db741727df182fa183d","label_status":"human-validated","meanings":[{"predictability":"predictable","sense_id":"oewn-mercurial__3.01.00.."},{"predictability":"not_predictable","sense_id":"oewn-mercurial__3.01.01.."},{"predictability":"predictable","sense_id":"oewn-mercurial__3.01.02.."},{"predictability":"not_predictable","sense_id":"oewn-mercurial__5.00.00.changeable.00"}],"morphology_disposition":"advance","note":"The meaning 'relating to or containing or caused by mercury' follows directly from the root 'mercury' (the metallic element) plus the adjectival suffix -al, which forms adjectives meaning 'relating to'. The meaning 'relating to or having characteristics attributed to the god Mercury' is not derivable from the root 'mercury' as the metallic element. It requires knowledge of the Roman god Mercury, which is not supplied by the root's recorded meanings. The meaning 'relating to or under the astrological influence of the planet Mercury' is not derivable from the root 'mercury' as the metallic element. It requires knowledge of the planet Mercury, which is not supplied by the root's recorded meanings. The meaning 'liable to sudden unpredictable change' is a figurative extension. While the root 'mercury' is a liquid metal, the sense of changeability is not directly given by the root's recorded meaning; it requires additional cultural or historical knowledge about mercury's properties or the god Mercury.","partition":"development","review_decision":"corrected","rubric_version":"morphology-rubric/2","slice":"meaning_shift_derivation","validated_at":"2026-08-30T06:54:08.893Z"}
